    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12762" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēfunctōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		defungor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>quickly despatched; slight, cursory</i> (post-Aug.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for class. negligens, levis): apodixis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 132, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ictus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 136, 5</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēfunctōrĭē</span></b> , <i>slightly, cursorily</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agere causam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 5, 31 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">petere aliquid,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					38, 17, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
